+# Broadcom research record
+
+Accessed 2026-08-15. These were the live Broadcom pages consulted for this design.
+
+| Page | Decision informed |
+|---|---|
+| [Update Sequence for VCF 9.0 and Compatible VMware Products](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/390634/) | Aria Suite Lifecycle must reach 8.18 Patch 2; Operations precedes Automation; Logs 9.0 is a fresh deployment and allows a Day-N transfer of up to 90 days. |
+| [Upgrading VMware Aria Operations 8.x to VCF Operations 9.0 using VMware Aria Suite Lifecycle](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/433805/) | Use the supported in-place Operations upgrade workflow and deploy Fleet Management as part of it. |
+| [Import and upgrade VMware Aria Automation 8.x to VCF Automation 9.0](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/433806/) | Import the existing Automation instance from legacy Aria Suite Lifecycle into Fleet Management before triggering the 9.0 upgrade. |
+| [Upgrade Guidance for Aria Operations for Logs 8.18.x to VCF Operations for Logs 9.0.x](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/402314/) | Run source and target Logs clusters in parallel, recreate integrations on the new deployment, and limit historical transfer to 90 days. |
+| [VCF Operations 9.0 Sizing Guidelines](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/397782/) | Select medium Operations analytics nodes, a standard unified cloud proxy, and a production Logs cluster of at least three medium nodes. |
+| [End of General Support for VMware Aria Operations 8.18](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/422643/) | Confirm that the exact inventoried VMware Aria Operations 8.18.3 release is governed by the 8.18 end-of-general-support boundary of 2027-10-11. |
+| [Build numbers and versions for VMware Aria Automation](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/318130/) | Confirm that the exact inventoried Automation 8.18.1 release has an end-of-general-support boundary of 2027-10-11. |
+| [Product Lifecycle matrix for Aria Suite](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/381187/) | Check the exact inventoried VMware Aria Operations for Logs 8.18.4 release under the 8.18 lifecycle entry and record its 2027-10-11 end-of-general-support boundary. |
+| [After upgrading Aria Automation 8.18 to VCF Automation 9.0.0.0](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/422762/) | Abandon legacy CSP login bookmarks and the vIDM login integration in favor of VCF Identity Broker routing. |
+| [Aria Operations Management Pack for Storage Devices unavailable from Broadcom Marketplace](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/429591/) | Abandon the inventoried Storage Devices management pack because support concluded with Aria Operations 8.18.3 and VCF Operations 9 uses integrated Storage Operations instead. |
+| [The Windows agent is not available when trying to download the client from within VMware Cloud Foundation Operations for Logs](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/402647/) | Retain compatible Logs 8.18 Windows agents and explicitly configure trust for the 9.0 target. |
+| [Upgrade of Aria Operations 8.18.6 or 8.18.7 to VCF Operations 9.0.x is Unsupported](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/438994/) | Confirm the newly published exclusion concerns 8.18.6/8.18.7, not the inventoried 8.18.3 source; never generalize 8.18.x compatibility without checking the exact patch version. |
+
+No consulted live source contradicted the pinned decisions for the exact inventoried versions. The pinned snapshot remains the deterministic artifact authority.
